n":[["OS","Windows 7 x64"],["Processor","AMD Athlon II X2 245 or higher/greater"],["Memory","2 GB RAM"],["Graphics","AMD Radeon HD 6450 or higher/greater"],["Sound Card","---"],["Additional Notes","---"]],"rec":[["OS","Windows 7x64"],["Processor","Intel Core2 Duo E6700 @ 2.66GHz or higher/greater"],["Memory","2 GB RAM"],["Graphics","GeForce GT 630 1G or higher/greater"]],"deck":2,"blurb":"As a young graffiti artist, you slip past police surveillance to spray walls in some of the world's best-known cities, including Paris, Tokyo, Berlin and New York. It is a turn-based infiltration game, so each level is a puzzle about timing and positioning, and the walls get harder to reach as you go.\n\nThe setting draws on real street art. You can bomb your tag, paint childlike figures or write poems in styles inspired by artists such as Blek Le Rat, Keith Haring, Lady Pink and Miss.Tic. Cosmografik developed it, with ARTE among its producers. It is single-player and suits puzzle and stealth fans with an interest in street art."}}